<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch bonds closed for holiday, reopen Dec 27.</title>
<headline>Dutch bonds closed for holiday, reopen Dec 27.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch bond market is closed for the Christmas holiday on December 26 and will reopen on Friday, December 27.</p>
<p>Bonds closed a touch higher on Tuesday's half-day trading session ahead of the holiday, with the 2006 bond up 0.11 to 102.12/20 for a 5.69 percent bid yield.</p>
<p>----Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
